# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.cache/

# NOTE: the assembled bundle output IS committed on purpose.
#
# `dsh plugin add github:AEmbers/dsh-orb-cordis` installs through a git dependency, and npm/pnpm run
# only the `prepare` lifecycle script for git installs — never `prepack`/`prepublishOnly`, and never a
# workspace-wide `pnpm build`. So if `packages/bundle/{lib,dist,client.js,package.json}` are not in the
# tree, the installed package has no `main` (`lib/index.js`), the install still succeeds silently, and
# the failure only shows up at boot.
#
# These entries used to be:
#   dist/
#   packages/*/lib/
#   packages/bundle/client.js
# They are relaxed here so the assembled `dsh-orb` package is installable straight from git.
# `packages/*/src` stays the source of truth; regenerate with `pnpm build` then
# `node packages/bundle/scripts/assemble.mjs`.
# (No `dist/` or `packages/*/lib/` rules remain — those directories now live in the tree on purpose.)

# Compiled from packages/*/src by `pnpm build` — never hand-edited.
#
# Also committed on purpose: the helper loads the syntax-highlighting grammars lazily at runtime
# (`packages/helper/assets/highlight.js` does `import('./vendor/shiki.js')`), and assembling the
# bundle only copies `packages/helper/assets` — so a tree without this directory ships a helper whose
# highlighting silently fails. `packages/*/src` remains the source of truth; regenerate with `pnpm build`.

